{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(guess)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (guess)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Just_2_min!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Just 2 min!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af23fb29681cfc6b84b3e9ffa4fac0dd18f2255b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{2\\pi}{11}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" /> What is the value of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb66360bc69b72e86eac3564c26bae7fd577bc9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin 3c \\cdot \\sin 6c \\cdot \\sin 9c \\cdot \\sin 12c \\cdot \\sin 15c}{\\sin c \\cdot \\sin 2c \\cdot \\sin 3c \\cdot \\sin 4c \\cdot \\sin 5c}?\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab849a826b1f0aec30d05749da6236b80591e8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ {-}1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ {-}\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{10}{11} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"449\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff84ea1918eb8039edc31877eb63ca11dfef1986.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin 3c \\cdot \\sin 6c \\cdot \\sin 9c \\cdot \\sin 12c \\cdot \\sin 15c}{\\sin c \\cdot \\sin 2c \\cdot \\sin 3c \\cdot \\sin 4c \\cdot \\sin 5c}=\\frac{\\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{12\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{18\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{24\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{30\\pi}{11}}{\\sin \\frac{2\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{4\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{8\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{10\\pi}{11}}.\\]\" width=\"615\" height=\"47\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64ec6f9758fa399c037d58e8237163761e75c0f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x+2\\pi)=\\sin(x),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/1660ef3b53656956bf1054d037d95261fe23f12c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(2\\pi-x)=\\sin(-x),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a523ef4147befc5fce5a30a4f9fad5677affa509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(-x)=-\\sin(x),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" /> we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/e/e7e5d4583710682a595b107182f40d55b4cad8b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{12\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{18\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{24\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{30\\pi}{11}}{\\sin \\frac{2\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{4\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{8\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{10\\pi}{11}}=\\frac{\\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{-10\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{-4\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{2\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{8\\pi}{11}}{\\sin \\frac{2\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{4\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{6\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{8\\pi}{11} \\cdot \\sin \\frac{10\\pi}{11}}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1}.\\]\" width=\"711\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>~kingofpineapplz\n~Ziyao7294 (minor edit)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Eisenstein used such a quotient in his proof of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_reciprocity\" title=\"Quadratic reciprocity\">quadratic reciprocity</a>. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/b/7cb6471b2a2b6be5826af87fa82064f5c6c9f477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\frac{2\\pi}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"58\" height=\"42\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is an odd prime number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is any integer.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95c02406e86d14d8772aa0d051c8699034e227a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sin(qc)\\sin(2qc)\\cdots\\sin(\\frac{p-1}{2}qc)}{\\sin(c)\\sin(2c)\\cdots\\sin(\\frac{p-1}{2}c)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"232\" height=\"50\" /> is the Legendre symbol <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea0989828d4c9510cca4c0c2addf368e9eec44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{q}{p}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"41\" height=\"45\" />. Legendre symbol is calculated using quadratic reciprocity which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c61a3e22866c892043f24f75a3f331824d93cde4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{p}{q}\\right)\\left(\\frac{q}{p}\\right)=(-1)^{\\frac{p-1}{2}\\frac{q-1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"190\" height=\"43\" />. The Legendre symbol <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa42615919303ad574ca02a432c05955b101ee4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{11}\\right)=(-1)\\left(\\frac{11}{3}\\right)=(-1)\\left(\\frac{-1}{3}\\right)=(-1)(-1)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"458\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>~Lopkiloinm\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d941d12a23d95a752574788081c91f55e9828066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"21\" />, so 3 is a quadratic residue mod 11. For quadratic residues, their Legendre symbol which we know is the answer from Solution 2 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc61a17c91dd9a768876dd86712a35c5852ba22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda38f45a64bbd4451aedeeb4584e01d91239172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"18\" /> be an 11th primitive root of unity. Then the quotient becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238aa3463016f1406f33d68e25ff8f077d5ca03a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(\\zeta^3-\\zeta^{-3})(\\zeta^6-\\zeta^{-6})(\\zeta^9-\\zeta^{-9})(\\zeta^{12}-\\zeta^{-12})(\\zeta^{15}-\\zeta^{-15})}{(\\zeta^1-\\zeta^{-1})(\\zeta^2-\\zeta^{-2})(\\zeta^3-\\zeta^{-3})(\\zeta^{4}-\\zeta^{-4})(\\zeta^{5}-\\zeta^{-5})}\\]\" width=\"428\" height=\"44\" /> which we can use modular arithmetic to become <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e6d07343b0ffc8642bd7ae054a801b3b8ec182.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(\\zeta^3-\\zeta^{-3})(\\zeta^{-5}-\\zeta^{5})(\\zeta^{-2}-\\zeta^{2})(\\zeta^{1}-\\zeta^{-1})(\\zeta^{4}-\\zeta^{-4})}{(\\zeta^1-\\zeta^{-1})(\\zeta^2-\\zeta^{-2})(\\zeta^3-\\zeta^{-3})(\\zeta^{4}-\\zeta^{-4})(\\zeta^{5}-\\zeta^{-5})}\\]\" width=\"401\" height=\"44\" /> and we see that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc61a17c91dd9a768876dd86712a35c5852ba22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Lopkiloinm\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28guess.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(guess)\">Solution 5 (guess)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (guess)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we can't calculate the exact value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/04148af912d102947a0bf1558ef0b7548e911f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\frac{2\\pi}{11}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" /> it's unlikely the answer will have radicals in it. This leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5baac6767e079700aa538f49b968da092e655c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1, 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfab6a5061c2b43f4d4604b51d0eb866a9cf4ded.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{11}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" /> The fraction is too precise for it to be a likely answer, so that leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/09352e06cfa1651aa82e838b91724b60b068d41d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> Note that if the angle is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f5bd922359ac3dfff1bc9a638d24fa6d32c39d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> the sine will be negative, and if it's less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> it'll be positive. The numerator and denominator are therefore both positive, so we eliminate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59ee4531d98c5fcd51688bc8eeae1235d4eb6865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"60\" height=\"30\" /> \n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Just_2_min.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Just_2_min!)\">Video Solution (Just 2 min!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Just 2 min!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/S44IzCpzTeg\">https://youtu.be/S44IzCpzTeg</a>\n</p><p>~<i>Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_.28English-Chinese_Bilingual.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\">Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7audWSKWf9U\">https://youtu.be/7audWSKWf9U</a>\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B\">2021 Fall AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.c